### 2020ApJ...901..151S: Molecular Gas Outflow in the Starburst Galaxy NGC 1482 (2020; nearby_galaxies; observational_alma_primary)
- question: What are the distribution, dynamics and energetics of molecular gas in the starburst-driven superwind of NGC 1482, and is the wind starburst driven?
- step 6: Outflow mass, energy, mass outflow rate
  - method: M_w from outflow CO flux with low X_CO; E=Mv^2/2; Mdot=v M/h_z with h_z=1 kpc [5.3 Dynamics: "For $h_z=1$ kpc, the distance that encompasses most of the outflow gas, Equation [\[eq:mor\]](#eq:mor) yields $\dot{M}_\mathrm{w}\sim7~M_\ensuremath{\odot}~\mathrm{yr}^{-1}$."]
  - assumption: X_CO=0.5e20, alpha_CO=1; cylindrical outflow, constant velocity, uniform density [5.3 Dynamics: "Applying a low CO-to-H$_2$ conversion factor of $X_\mathrm{CO}=0.5\times10^{20}\mathrm{cm^{-2}(K~km~s^{-1})^{-1}}$"]
  - validation: Cylinder geometry gives conservative estimate versus spherical [5.3 Dynamics: "we adopt the cylinder geometry that gives a conservative estimate of $\dot{M}_\mathrm{w}$."]
- result: Outflow CO flux = ~70 ± ~30% Jy km/s [5.3 Dynamics: "$\int S_\mathrm{CO}\mathrm{d}v\approx70~\mathrm{Jy~km~s^{-1}}$ with an uncertainty of $\approx30\%$"]
- result: Outflow mass = ~7e7 ± not stated Msun [5.3 Dynamics: "$M_\mathrm{w}\sim7\times10^7~M_\ensuremath{\odot}$"]
- result: Outflow kinetic energy = ~7e54 ± not stated erg [5.3 Dynamics: "$E_\mathrm{w}=M_\mathrm{w}v_\mathrm{w}^2/2\sim7\times10^{54}~\mathrm{erg}$"]
